1
00:00:27,902 --> 00:00:29,028
Sophie.

2
00:00:30,112 --> 00:00:32,323
Do you think you could
persuade your sister

3
00:00:32,448 --> 00:00:34,825
to make at least
a token appearance?

4
00:00:35,284 --> 00:00:36,452
I doubt it.

5
00:00:36,911 --> 00:00:37,954
Please try.

6
00:00:38,538 --> 00:00:39,830
- Sure, mom.
- Okay.

7
00:00:41,457 --> 00:00:43,834
Oh, how are you?
Good to see you.

8
00:00:44,377 --> 00:00:45,920
My condolences.

9
00:00:52,301 --> 00:00:53,344
Abs?

10
00:00:59,308 --> 00:01:00,351
Abs?

11
00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:03,688
Abby, are you awake?

12
00:01:13,573 --> 00:01:15,324
- Okay, go ahead.
- Yeah, I'm on my way.

13
00:01:19,412 --> 00:01:20,454
Yeah.
All right. All right.

14
00:01:20,580 --> 00:01:21,789
I'm heading through
the front entrance right now.

15
00:01:21,914 --> 00:01:23,207
What's your 20?

16
00:01:28,421 --> 00:01:29,463
Hey, boss.

17
00:01:29,964 --> 00:01:32,592
Victim's name is Austin Marr.
23. Multiple stab wounds.

18
00:01:32,717 --> 00:01:34,552
Killed in the guesthouse
last night around 2:00 A.M.

19
00:01:35,011 --> 00:01:36,220
What's with all the security?

20
00:01:36,512 --> 00:01:37,722
Well, the house belongs
to a federal judge

21
00:01:37,847 --> 00:01:38,931
named Pauline Fitzwilliam.

22
00:01:39,056 --> 00:01:41,309
Her mother just died.
A lot of VIPs are here for the wake.

23
00:01:41,475 --> 00:01:43,978
- Stiff security for a wake.
- Where's Jane?

24
00:01:44,353 --> 00:01:46,063
Who knows? He can catch up
when he gets here.

25
00:01:46,439 --> 00:01:48,649
Metal items
in the plastic container, please

26
00:01:53,738 --> 00:01:54,947
I was looking for Abby.

27
00:01:55,114 --> 00:01:57,033
I didn't even know
Austin was in the house.

28
00:01:57,366 --> 00:01:59,035
- He doesn't live here?
- No.

29
00:01:59,869 --> 00:02:01,162
He's Abby's boyfriend.

30
00:02:01,996 --> 00:02:03,623
He's sweet and gentle.

31
00:02:04,498 --> 00:02:05,875
Who would do this to him?

32
00:02:07,835 --> 00:02:09,837
I need you to stay with me, Sophie.

33
00:02:11,130 --> 00:02:12,173
Okay.

34
00:02:12,298 --> 00:02:13,924
Does Austin have family
in the area?

35
00:02:14,634 --> 00:02:15,676
No.

36
00:02:16,135 --> 00:02:17,678
Sophie, do you know
where Austin works?

37
00:02:18,638 --> 00:02:20,431
I'm not sure. He's...

38
00:02:21,390 --> 00:02:24,018
He's an illustrator
for children's books.

39
00:02:24,435 --> 00:02:25,895
And how was
his relationship with Abby?

40
00:02:27,480 --> 00:02:28,564
They were in love.

41
00:02:29,065 --> 00:02:30,483
Austin treated her like gold.

42
00:02:31,567 --> 00:02:33,444
When was the last time
you saw your sister?

43
00:02:34,278 --> 00:02:35,404
Yesterday afternoon.

44
00:02:36,530 --> 00:02:38,115
Where is she?
What's happened to her?

45
00:02:38,616 --> 00:02:40,201
That's what we're trying
to figure out.

46
00:02:40,534 --> 00:02:43,037
We'll let you know as soon
as we find anything out.

47
00:02:43,704 --> 00:02:45,206
- Thank you for your time.
- But she's okay, right?

48
00:02:45,331 --> 00:02:47,124
'Cause she's my baby sister.

49
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:49,043
- We'll let you know.
- Okay.

50
00:02:51,921 --> 00:02:53,047
I talked to security.

51
00:02:53,214 --> 00:02:55,257
They say they've got a sealed
perimeter around the estate.

52
00:02:55,383 --> 00:02:57,385
No one goes in or out
unless it's through them.

53
00:02:58,135 --> 00:03:00,721
Abby came in yesterday morning
at 8:40, but there's no record

54
00:03:00,930 --> 00:03:01,972
that she left.

55
00:03:02,348 --> 00:03:03,724
So she's still in the house?

56
00:03:04,016 --> 00:03:07,144
That's the thing. Local PD and security
searched the property...

57
00:03:07,311 --> 00:03:09,897
every building, every room.
They can't find her anywhere.

58
00:03:10,022 --> 00:03:11,190
Well, maybe she left
with someone.

59
00:03:11,315 --> 00:03:13,359
Security's saying no.
They check everyone that leaves.

60
00:03:13,484 --> 00:03:14,819
They even search their cars.

61
00:03:15,027 --> 00:03:18,072
So Abby's missing, but security
says she never left?

62
00:03:18,364 --> 00:03:19,740
I was having such a good day.

63
00:03:20,032 --> 00:03:24,078
Cho, check out Austin...
home, work, other friends.

64
00:03:24,870 --> 00:03:27,289
Van Pelt, get with security.
I want the names of everybody

65
00:03:27,415 --> 00:03:30,292
who was on the property at the time
of death, and I wanna talk to 'em.

66
00:03:30,418 --> 00:03:31,836
- On it.
- Uh, and if you see Jane

67
00:03:31,961 --> 00:03:33,379
tell him he's officially tardy.

68
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:38,008
"Sir, all metals items
in the plastic bin, please."

69
00:03:38,676 --> 00:03:39,719
"Sir, please step back."

70
00:03:40,052 --> 00:03:41,804
Uh, I'm with CBI.

71
00:03:41,971 --> 00:03:43,639
I'm in a hurry.
I'm just gonna go around.

72
00:03:43,764 --> 00:03:45,725
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.
Where's your badge?

73
00:03:46,308 --> 00:03:48,269
- You just grabbed my arm.
- Oh, maybe you didn't hear me.

74
00:03:48,394 --> 00:03:50,646
Marcus Whiteside, Security Chief here.
Where's your badge?

75
00:03:52,189 --> 00:03:53,441
- That's my badge.
- Okay, then. Now...

76
00:03:53,566 --> 00:03:54,650
- go through the gate.
- Where's your badge?

77
00:03:54,859 --> 00:03:57,319
- Are we gonna have a problem here?
- No. Not at all. I'm just asking.

78
00:03:57,486 --> 00:03:58,529
Through the gate.

79
00:03:58,654 --> 00:04:00,364
I'm one of the good guys here, man.
I'm... I'm here to help.

80
00:04:00,489 --> 00:04:03,826
Family, friends, CBI... everyone goes
through the gate. Got it?

81
00:04:03,993 --> 00:04:05,661
I got it. That means you go
through the gate, too?

82
00:04:05,786 --> 00:04:07,079
- Absolutely.
- Okay.

83
00:04:08,164 --> 00:04:11,041
Marcus, please, be my guest.
After you. The least I could do.

84
00:04:40,780 --> 00:04:42,156
Uh, you know, I-I may...

85
00:04:42,281 --> 00:04:44,366
Can I just... please?
Thank you.

86
00:04:48,913 --> 00:04:49,955
Seems to be working.

87
00:05:04,384 --> 00:05:06,553
"Come on. I want a bite.
Come on. Just give me a bite."

88
00:05:06,720 --> 00:05:07,763
- "No. You don't deserve it."
- "I just want one..."

89
00:05:07,888 --> 00:05:09,431
"Well, maybe I'm just gonna
have to take it then."

90
00:05:09,556 --> 00:05:11,892
"Then take it. No?"

91
00:05:15,771 --> 00:05:17,981
{\an8}- "I love you so much."
- "I love you, too."

92
00:05:18,190 --> 00:05:19,900
{\an8}"Oh. You hear that?
She loves me."

93
00:05:23,445 --> 00:05:24,613
I know what's happened here.

94
00:05:26,448 --> 00:05:27,658
What's that, judge?

95
00:05:29,284 --> 00:05:31,787
Three months ago, I sentenced
a man named Raymond Tubbs

96
00:05:31,912 --> 00:05:33,580
to 40 years without parole.

97
00:05:34,248 --> 00:05:36,041
{\an8}He's a white supremacist
runs a gang

98
00:05:36,166 --> 00:05:38,210
{\an8}that's been robbing banks
up and down the coast.

99
00:05:38,919 --> 00:05:42,756
{\an8}Mr. Tubbs swore he would kill me
and my family so obviously...

100
00:05:43,423 --> 00:05:45,217
{\an8}someone working for him

101
00:05:45,467 --> 00:05:48,178
{\an8}killed poor Austin
and took Abby.

102
00:05:48,762 --> 00:05:51,557
{\an8}But your security team says
nobody entered the compound.

103
00:05:51,765 --> 00:05:53,767
Well, they also said
Abby must still be here

104
00:05:53,892 --> 00:05:55,269
{\an8}and they've searched
and haven't found her

105
00:05:55,435 --> 00:05:59,314
{\an8}so obviously they're wrong
in some respects.

106
00:05:59,982 --> 00:06:01,275
{\an8}Where's Tubbs doing time?

107
00:06:01,984 --> 00:06:04,820
{\an8}Folsom.
That doesn't stop him.

108
00:06:05,362 --> 00:06:07,948
{\an8}Last month he sent a member of
his gang to break into our house.

109
00:06:08,115 --> 00:06:10,325
{\an8}That's when we stepped up security.

110
00:06:11,076 --> 00:06:14,746
{\an8}Did your forensics get anything
from the crime scene?

111
00:06:15,330 --> 00:06:17,749
{\an8}Ma'am, we prefer not to give
details of our investigation

112
00:06:17,875 --> 00:06:20,002
{\an8}- until it's compl...
- Agent, I was a DA for 12 years.

113
00:06:20,127 --> 00:06:22,170
I can pick up the phone
and find out what you've got

114
00:06:22,379 --> 00:06:23,964
or you can just tell me.

115
00:06:25,007 --> 00:06:27,426
{\an8}Partial prints on the murder weapon
and Austin's blood.

116
00:06:27,676 --> 00:06:29,803
{\an8}- We're running it now.
- Fine.

117
00:06:30,220 --> 00:06:32,598
{\an8}You'll find that it belongs
to someone working for Tubbs.

118
00:06:32,723 --> 00:06:35,434
{\an8}You track him, you will find Abby.

119
00:06:36,476 --> 00:06:37,603
{\an8}We'll look into Tubbs

120
00:06:37,936 --> 00:06:40,439
{\an8}but there are other avenues
to explore.

121
00:06:41,356 --> 00:06:42,399
Such as?

122
00:06:42,941 --> 00:06:44,902
Ma'am, as a matter of course

123
00:06:45,110 --> 00:06:47,029
we looked
into Abby's background.

124
00:06:47,446 --> 00:06:50,032
She has issues
with drug and alcohol abuse.

125
00:06:50,532 --> 00:06:51,575
Had issues.

126
00:06:52,075 --> 00:06:55,454
She's been clean for months and what
has that to do with this situation?

127
00:06:55,787 --> 00:06:58,165
Parents aren't always the first
to know about a relapse

128
00:06:58,290 --> 00:07:00,292
and drug dealers
are dangerous company.

129
00:07:00,459 --> 00:07:01,835
Abby was clean and sober.

130
00:07:02,336 --> 00:07:04,338
{\an8}- And Austin?
- He was the same.

131
00:07:05,172 --> 00:07:06,924
{\an8}And how was
their relationship lately?

132
00:07:07,215 --> 00:07:08,467
It was good.

133
00:07:09,384 --> 00:07:11,428
{\an8}There were wounds
on his face...

134
00:07:12,304 --> 00:07:15,599
{\an8}fingernail scratches which suggests
he had a fight with a female

135
00:07:15,724 --> 00:07:17,351
shortly before he was killed.

136
00:07:21,063 --> 00:07:22,564
Are you suggesting

137
00:07:23,357 --> 00:07:26,526
{\an8}that Abby fought with Austin
and then killed him?

138
00:07:26,735 --> 00:07:29,863
{\an8}Like I said, ma'am
other avenues to explore.

139
00:07:31,865 --> 00:07:33,659
Agent, if my daughter
comes to harm

140
00:07:33,784 --> 00:07:35,202
because you frittered away
your time

141
00:07:35,327 --> 00:07:38,205
looking into her personal life
your career is over.

142
00:07:38,330 --> 00:07:39,831
Do you understand me?

143
00:07:41,416 --> 00:07:45,379
Ma'am, I understand your distress
during this difficult time

144
00:07:45,837 --> 00:07:47,923
but we'll go wherever
this investigation takes us.

145
00:07:48,048 --> 00:07:49,216
It's my duty.

146
00:07:51,927 --> 00:07:52,970
Ah.

147
00:08:17,202 --> 00:08:18,286
Can I help you?

148
00:08:18,662 --> 00:08:19,830
Well, that depends.

149
00:08:21,039 --> 00:08:22,082
Who are you?

150
00:08:22,666 --> 00:08:24,918
- Ed Saban.
- Uh, I just...

151
00:08:25,377 --> 00:08:28,046
- And you are?
- Patrick Jane, CBI.

152
00:08:28,547 --> 00:08:30,924
Oh, I-I spoke with one
of your colleagues, uh...

153
00:08:31,883 --> 00:08:33,218
Van Pelt, I believe.

154
00:08:33,593 --> 00:08:35,470
Does that mean you've had
enough of questions?

155
00:08:35,804 --> 00:08:37,431
- Uh... No. That... that's not what I...
- Good.

156
00:08:37,556 --> 00:08:38,890
Where were you last night?

157
00:08:40,517 --> 00:08:41,893
Uh... here.

158
00:08:42,144 --> 00:08:43,729
Uh, i-i-in bed. I...

159
00:08:44,813 --> 00:08:49,401
I was tired from working all day
and took a sleeping pill.

160
00:08:54,031 --> 00:08:55,073
Hmm.

161
00:08:56,408 --> 00:08:57,534
I'm not actually a cop.

162
00:08:59,036 --> 00:09:02,080
I'm what you, uh, would refer
to as a...

163
00:09:02,956 --> 00:09:04,791
- consultant.
- Oh.

164
00:09:06,334 --> 00:09:07,669
- Funny.
- No.

165
00:09:08,086 --> 00:09:10,839
You have a distinctly medical air.

166
00:09:12,090 --> 00:09:13,675
Are you a family doctor?

167
00:09:13,884 --> 00:09:18,138
Uh, Ethel's. I, uh, I took care
of her the last year or so.

168
00:09:18,638 --> 00:09:20,474
- Oops.
- Ethel was 93.

169
00:09:20,599 --> 00:09:21,892
I think all things considered

170
00:09:22,017 --> 00:09:24,853
we gave her
a reasonably peaceful end.

171
00:09:27,439 --> 00:09:29,107
So what do you think's
happened to Abby?

172
00:09:29,483 --> 00:09:30,525
Who?

173
00:09:31,318 --> 00:09:34,321
Abigail Fitzwilliam...
Ethel's granddaughter.

174
00:09:34,446 --> 00:09:36,156
Oh, Abby. Yeah.
What about her?

175
00:09:37,282 --> 00:09:39,868
- She's missing, isn't she?
- Is she?

176
00:09:40,619 --> 00:09:41,661
Do the police know?

177
00:09:43,121 --> 00:09:44,581
- You're joking again.
- Yes.

178
00:09:48,126 --> 00:09:50,587
- How would you describe Abby?
- Oh, uh...

179
00:09:50,712 --> 00:09:53,882
A good-hearted young woman.

180
00:09:55,425 --> 00:09:57,761
Full of life. Vivacious.

181
00:09:58,887 --> 00:10:00,806
Oh. Uh, excuse me.
I have a...

182
00:10:01,932 --> 00:10:03,350
Um, please?

183
00:10:03,475 --> 00:10:04,518
Oh.

184
00:10:08,146 --> 00:10:09,189
Lisbon, hello.

185
00:10:09,314 --> 00:10:10,440
Jane, where are you?

186
00:10:10,941 --> 00:10:13,235
I'm just talking
with the family doctor here.

187
00:10:13,819 --> 00:10:16,780
He says our missing girl is an unstable
nymphomaniacal stoner.

188
00:10:16,905 --> 00:10:18,573
- Interesting, no?
- Uh, I didn't say that.

189
00:10:18,698 --> 00:10:20,450
Yes, you did.
You practically screamed it.

190
00:10:20,617 --> 00:10:22,452
I'm at the front door now.
Meet me here.

191
00:10:22,661 --> 00:10:25,205
Yeah. I-I'll be right there.
Thanks for your time.

192
00:10:28,625 --> 00:10:29,668
"No sign of the girl?"

193
00:10:29,793 --> 00:10:32,587
"No, and the security people say she
couldn't have possibly left the property"

194
00:10:32,712 --> 00:10:33,839
"without their knowledge."

195
00:10:34,339 --> 00:10:36,758
We should see if she was sleeping
with any of the security people.

196
00:10:36,967 --> 00:10:39,928
It's a thought. And the mom
says neo-Nazis staged a raid

197
00:10:40,137 --> 00:10:43,306
but security said nobody came
on the property so puzzle that out.

198
00:10:43,765 --> 00:10:44,808
Give me a minute.

199
00:10:45,267 --> 00:10:47,602
Cho. Yeah, I need you
to check out Raymond Tubbs.

200
00:10:47,727 --> 00:10:49,646
He's in federal prison in Folsom.

201
00:10:50,147 --> 00:10:52,357
Yeah, talk to him, see what he knows
about the Fitzwilliams.

202
00:10:52,482 --> 00:10:54,442
Also, did you get anything
on those fingerprints?

203
00:10:54,776 --> 00:10:55,819
Let me know.

204
00:10:56,069 --> 00:10:57,362
Okay. Minute's up.
What's the answer?

205
00:10:57,487 --> 00:10:58,864
That was not a minute. That was...

206
00:10:59,114 --> 00:11:00,657
- less than 30 seconds, even.
- Reasonably

207
00:11:00,782 --> 00:11:02,993
Agent Lisbon, you said that, um...

208
00:11:03,285 --> 00:11:04,828
if you found anything
you'd let me know.

209
00:11:05,495 --> 00:11:07,414
- Have you?
- No, Sophie. I'm sorry.

210
00:11:07,539 --> 00:11:08,582
I got it.

211
00:11:08,915 --> 00:11:09,958
- What?
- You asked me to puzzle it out.

212
00:11:10,083 --> 00:11:12,294
- I puzzled it out.
- What? What is it?

213
00:11:12,419 --> 00:11:13,962
Uh, well, there's been
no ransom demand

214
00:11:14,087 --> 00:11:15,422
so that rules out abduction

215
00:11:15,755 --> 00:11:17,757
leaves three options
for your sister's disappearance.

216
00:11:17,883 --> 00:11:23,054
One, she was killed and her body
was removed from the compound.

217
00:11:23,180 --> 00:11:26,141
Two, she was killed and her body
was hidden on the compound.

218
00:11:26,391 --> 00:11:29,436
Or three, she killed Austin
and fled the scene.

219
00:11:30,103 --> 00:11:31,188
No, that can't be.

220
00:11:32,063 --> 00:11:33,106
You're hiding something.

221
00:11:33,857 --> 00:11:35,317
What? No?

222
00:11:35,942 --> 00:11:37,986
Obviously something
about your sister. What is it?

223
00:11:39,738 --> 00:11:42,157
- No.
- Oh, come on. You can tell me.

224
00:11:43,158 --> 00:11:44,284
You don't know Abby.

225
00:11:44,826 --> 00:11:46,578
She would never hurt Austin.

226
00:11:46,828 --> 00:11:49,331
You wanna believe that but you know
it's not true, don't you?

227
00:11:50,207 --> 00:11:52,125
You ever notice that feeling

228
00:11:52,250 --> 00:11:53,919
that physical unwell feeling
you get

229
00:11:54,044 --> 00:11:56,463
when you know you should say
or do something and you don't?

230
00:11:57,005 --> 00:11:59,049
Heart pounds
headache, backache.

231
00:12:00,717 --> 00:12:02,469
You can feel better...

232
00:12:03,178 --> 00:12:05,722
immediately
if you tell the truth.

233
00:12:08,099 --> 00:12:09,142
Right now.

234
00:12:11,895 --> 00:12:13,897
Yesterday I went to
the guesthouse to see Abby.

235
00:12:14,022 --> 00:12:15,065
Mm-hmm.

236
00:12:15,732 --> 00:12:17,901
Austin was there
and they were arguing.

237
00:12:18,610 --> 00:12:19,986
I have never seen them like that.

238
00:12:21,696 --> 00:12:22,864
Abby tried to leave

239
00:12:23,281 --> 00:12:25,450
and Austin started
to shake her

240
00:12:26,284 --> 00:12:28,495
and he was yelling at her
and shaking her.

241
00:12:28,787 --> 00:12:29,913
What did Abby do?

242
00:12:30,830 --> 00:12:32,999
- She hit him in the face.
- Yeah.

243
00:12:33,625 --> 00:12:34,668
He was bleeding.

244
00:12:36,044 --> 00:12:37,087
Then what happened?

245
00:12:37,879 --> 00:12:39,089
I don't know. I left.

246
00:12:40,465 --> 00:12:41,508
Excuse me.

247
00:12:42,467 --> 00:12:44,719
Of course.
Well, thank you, Sophie.

248
00:12:45,720 --> 00:12:46,972
That was very valuable.

249
00:12:47,389 --> 00:12:48,556
Now you should take
a little lie-down

250
00:12:48,682 --> 00:12:50,058
maybe catch up on some sleep.

251
00:12:50,976 --> 00:12:52,018
Okay.

252
00:12:53,270 --> 00:12:54,980
When you wake up
you're gonna feel a lot better.

253
00:12:57,399 --> 00:12:58,441
Thank you.

254
00:12:59,067 --> 00:13:00,735
Forensics got a match
from the prints

255
00:13:00,860 --> 00:13:02,404
from the knife that was used
as the murder weapon.

256
00:13:02,737 --> 00:13:03,780
They're Abby's.

257
00:13:09,077 --> 00:13:10,954
"I'm telling you, Abby did not leave
that compound."

258
00:13:11,288 --> 00:13:13,373
You and your men searched
the house and the grounds.

259
00:13:13,498 --> 00:13:14,541
She wasn't there?

260
00:13:15,208 --> 00:13:16,960
Is it possible that there's a hole
in the system?

261
00:13:17,460 --> 00:13:19,838
There are cameras, regular patrols,
and motion sensors.

262
00:13:19,963 --> 00:13:21,006
It's just not possible.

263
00:13:21,131 --> 00:13:22,465
We'll have to search
the place again is all.

264
00:13:22,590 --> 00:13:24,676
- We must've missed her.
- First things first

265
00:13:24,884 --> 00:13:27,012
could somebody in the family
have helped Abby escape?

266
00:13:27,178 --> 00:13:29,014
None of them have access
to the security system

267
00:13:29,139 --> 00:13:30,348
not even Pauline.

268
00:13:31,016 --> 00:13:33,518
What about your men?
Are any of them vulnerabilities?

269
00:13:34,185 --> 00:13:36,438
They're ex-military
and law enforcement.

270
00:13:36,855 --> 00:13:38,398
I handpicked them myself.

271
00:13:38,982 --> 00:13:40,066
We're gonna need a list
of their names.

272
00:13:40,191 --> 00:13:41,276
You're wasting your time.

273
00:13:41,985 --> 00:13:43,028
You should be talking
to all the people

274
00:13:43,153 --> 00:13:45,447
who were on the compound
when Austin was killed.

275
00:13:45,655 --> 00:13:48,742
We have talked to them.
Six in total, not including Abby...

276
00:13:49,075 --> 00:13:53,496
Pauline, Sophie, Ed Saban
two maids, Ethel's cousin Ruth.

277
00:13:54,164 --> 00:13:55,707
We're looking into all of them
but right now

278
00:13:55,832 --> 00:13:57,876
what I am interested in
is finding Abby.

279
00:14:00,837 --> 00:14:02,130
So Abby and Austin
have a fight

280
00:14:02,255 --> 00:14:03,465
and then later on
that night, she kills him?

281
00:14:03,590 --> 00:14:04,716
That's what it looks like.

282
00:14:04,883 --> 00:14:06,593
Still doesn't explain
how she got off the estate.

283
00:14:07,260 --> 00:14:09,346
When we find Abby
we'll have our answer.

284
00:14:09,721 --> 00:14:12,057
Whiteside sent me a list
of the names of his security team.

285
00:14:12,223 --> 00:14:14,351
Run background checks on them.
See if anything comes up.

286
00:14:14,476 --> 00:14:15,727
- Yeah, you got it.
- Hey, boss.

287
00:14:16,019 --> 00:14:17,270
Abby Fitzwilliam used her credit card

288
00:14:17,395 --> 00:14:19,481
three hours ago at a boutique
in San Francisco.

289
00:14:19,647 --> 00:14:21,107
The store faxed over
an itemized receipt.

290
00:14:21,274 --> 00:14:22,317
Let's go check it out.

291
00:14:24,194 --> 00:14:25,695
"Marin Life" magazine?

292
00:14:27,238 --> 00:14:28,281
It's a good read.

293
00:14:28,948 --> 00:14:31,201
Abby liked to party
just like the doctor said.

294
00:14:31,368 --> 00:14:33,536
She and her posse
are all through this.

295
00:14:34,954 --> 00:14:38,208
- The point is...
- I'm exploring the world of the suspect.

296
00:14:38,500 --> 00:14:40,668
Well, you enjoy exploring.

297
00:14:40,919 --> 00:14:43,046
We'll go get on her trail
and arrest her.

298
00:14:43,296 --> 00:14:45,924
- What did Abby buy at the store?
- Um...

299
00:14:46,841 --> 00:14:49,260
skirt suit, blazer
and a Tumi bag. Why?

300
00:14:49,844 --> 00:14:50,887
No reason.

301
00:14:55,016 --> 00:14:56,643
She was in a few hours ago.

302
00:14:57,894 --> 00:14:59,854
- Okay...
- She spent $800

303
00:14:59,979 --> 00:15:01,898
on a skirt suit
blazer, and a handbag.

304
00:15:02,941 --> 00:15:05,402
- Okay...
- Here's her picture.

305
00:15:06,027 --> 00:15:08,613
Oh, yeah. I remember.
Blonder, though.

306
00:15:08,780 --> 00:15:10,281
- Was she with anyone?
- No.

307
00:15:10,740 --> 00:15:12,200
Do you remember
anything else about her?

308
00:15:12,742 --> 00:15:13,952
Fierce shoes.

309
00:15:14,994 --> 00:15:18,039
Oh! She left an address.
Jacket needed altering.

310
00:15:19,124 --> 00:15:20,166
Do you want it?

311
00:15:21,126 --> 00:15:22,168
Yes.

312
00:15:27,257 --> 00:15:29,884
Put your badge away. If she thinks
we're cops she might run.

313
00:15:30,135 --> 00:15:31,261
I don't feel like running.

314
00:15:35,014 --> 00:15:37,517
Hi. We have
a delivery from L Couturier.

315
00:15:37,684 --> 00:15:39,352
- You wanna open the door?
- "She's lying."

316
00:15:41,479 --> 00:15:43,606
- Abby Fitzwilliam, you're under arrest.
- I'm not Abby.

317
00:15:45,108 --> 00:15:46,693
Put your hands in the air now!

318
00:15:46,985 --> 00:15:49,070
Lisbon, Grace
where's your manners?

319
00:15:49,237 --> 00:15:51,114
This is Daniella,
Abby's best friend.

320
00:15:52,073 --> 00:15:53,741
Come in. Have a seat.

321
00:16:05,418 --> 00:16:07,628
Okay. You win.
How'd you find Daniella?

322
00:16:07,753 --> 00:16:08,796
What's my prize?

323
00:16:09,297 --> 00:16:11,966
Abby Fitzwilliam is a party girl
with a rebellious streak.

324
00:16:12,508 --> 00:16:14,677
She dresses like one.
Lots of animal prints.

325
00:16:14,927 --> 00:16:17,847
- The receipt.
- Skirt suit, blazer, Tumi bag.

326
00:16:18,723 --> 00:16:19,849
Very east coast prep.

327
00:16:20,183 --> 00:16:21,976
No way Abby would've bought
any of that.

328
00:16:22,143 --> 00:16:23,394
Daniella is the only one
of Abby's friends

329
00:16:23,519 --> 00:16:25,563
with that, uh
appropriate sense of style.

330
00:16:25,771 --> 00:16:27,482
- How'd you find her?
- ESP.

331
00:16:28,733 --> 00:16:30,151
No, I had Cho look up
her address.

332
00:16:32,695 --> 00:16:34,113
Why did you steal
Abby's credit card?

333
00:16:34,864 --> 00:16:36,991
I didn't. She loaned it to me.

334
00:16:38,284 --> 00:16:39,327
She was a good friend.

335
00:16:40,703 --> 00:16:42,038
I have friends, Daniella.

336
00:16:42,330 --> 00:16:43,789
I don't loan them
my credit card.

337
00:16:44,499 --> 00:16:46,334
Well, what can I say?
Abby is generous.

338
00:16:47,710 --> 00:16:49,378
I have a job interview
in a few days.

339
00:16:50,505 --> 00:16:52,089
She said I needed to look
my best.

340
00:16:53,841 --> 00:16:55,343
She always helped me
when I needed it.

341
00:16:56,719 --> 00:16:58,513
Even if I said no
she wouldn't listen.

342
00:17:00,014 --> 00:17:01,057
It's true.

343
00:17:01,182 --> 00:17:03,017
Ask around. She did it
for lots of people.

344
00:17:03,184 --> 00:17:04,435
When did she give you
the card?

345
00:17:05,311 --> 00:17:08,147
Um... three days ago.

346
00:17:08,814 --> 00:17:10,233
The day before she went missing?

347
00:17:12,026 --> 00:17:13,903
Abby called me and told me
her grandma was really sick

348
00:17:14,028 --> 00:17:15,780
and that she wasn't gonna last
much longer.

349
00:17:17,448 --> 00:17:18,699
I went over to be with her.

350
00:17:19,325 --> 00:17:21,452
- How'd she seem?
- She was sad.

351
00:17:23,204 --> 00:17:24,247
Crying a lot.

352
00:17:25,873 --> 00:17:27,416
She and her grandma
were really close.

353
00:17:31,837 --> 00:17:33,089
And she was drinking.

354
00:17:34,465 --> 00:17:36,008
"It was... it was just wine but still."

355
00:17:36,968 --> 00:17:38,511
I told her I didn't think
it was a good idea.

356
00:17:39,595 --> 00:17:41,264
You know, she had problems
with that kinda stuff.

357
00:17:42,181 --> 00:17:43,224
Was Austin there?

358
00:17:43,599 --> 00:17:45,476
No. Abby wouldn't have been
drinking if he was.

359
00:17:46,394 --> 00:17:49,313
Austin's totally straight-edged.
He got her sober.

360
00:17:50,147 --> 00:17:51,774
The night Abby went missing
where were you?

361
00:17:52,733 --> 00:17:54,068
In L.A. for work.

362
00:17:55,820 --> 00:17:57,280
Boss, need you out here.

363
00:18:04,412 --> 00:18:06,789
I said Mr. Jane.
I wanna talk to Mr. Jane.

364
00:18:06,956 --> 00:18:08,291
- Where is he?
- I turned my back for a second.

365
00:18:08,416 --> 00:18:09,458
You know how he is.

366
00:18:09,584 --> 00:18:11,669
He's not here right now, Sophie.
What's the problem?

367
00:18:12,295 --> 00:18:14,589
I, um, I got this message.

368
00:18:15,381 --> 00:18:16,465
I don't know what it means.

369
00:18:16,632 --> 00:18:18,134
What message?
What are you talking about?

370
00:18:18,634 --> 00:18:20,094
"Tell your bitch mom
that's what she gets"

371
00:18:20,219 --> 00:18:21,679
"for messing
with Raymond Tubbs."

372
00:18:21,971 --> 00:18:23,931
"Your sister and her friend
were just the beginning."

373
00:18:24,223 --> 00:18:26,726
"You will reap the whirlwind.
Eight, eight."

374
00:18:27,518 --> 00:18:29,103
I've never heard
that voice before.

375
00:18:29,687 --> 00:18:30,813
"Eight, eight"?
What does that mean?

376
00:18:31,022 --> 00:18:32,523
It's a code used
by white supremacists.

377
00:18:32,690 --> 00:18:35,234
The eighth letter of the alphabet
"HH", "Heil Hitler."

378
00:18:35,443 --> 00:18:37,987
It's blocked. Sophie we're gonna need
your phone for a little while.

379
00:18:38,195 --> 00:18:39,405
- Get a trace on it.
- Yeah, you got it.

380
00:18:39,530 --> 00:18:40,573
You said Abby did this.

381
00:18:40,781 --> 00:18:42,617
You said her fingerprint
was on the knife.

382
00:18:42,742 --> 00:18:44,076
We don't know what this means

383
00:18:44,201 --> 00:18:45,536
but right now
you shouldn't be alone.

384
00:18:45,661 --> 00:18:47,204
I'm gonna have
an agent bring you home.

385
00:18:47,538 --> 00:18:50,166
What about Abby? Did these people
do something to her?

386
00:18:50,333 --> 00:18:51,917
That's what we're gonna find out.
Come with me.

387
00:18:52,043 --> 00:18:53,085
Okay.

388
00:19:00,343 --> 00:19:01,385
Raymond Tubbs?

389
00:19:01,927 --> 00:19:03,054
Yeah. Who are you?

390
00:19:03,429 --> 00:19:04,930
I'm Agent Cho from the CBI.

391
00:19:05,973 --> 00:19:08,100
I'd like to ask you a few questions
about Pauline Fitzwilliam.

392
00:19:09,935 --> 00:19:10,978
What about her?

393
00:19:11,437 --> 00:19:13,272
A man was killed
on the Fitzwilliam compound.

394
00:19:13,481 --> 00:19:14,690
A family member is missing.

395
00:19:15,399 --> 00:19:17,151
Another family member
received a voice mail.

396
00:19:18,361 --> 00:19:20,529
It said, "That's what you get
for messing with Raymond Tubbs."

397
00:19:23,115 --> 00:19:24,575
Leadership's a bitch, huh?

398
00:19:24,867 --> 00:19:26,327
You try to keep your folks
on point

399
00:19:26,452 --> 00:19:28,496
and then some darn fool
opens his mouth.

400
00:19:29,705 --> 00:19:31,207
Where you hail
from Agent Cho?

401
00:19:32,124 --> 00:19:33,167
Oakland.

402
00:19:34,627 --> 00:19:35,670
Okay.

403
00:19:35,795 --> 00:19:37,421
- Where are your parents from?
- Korea.

404
00:19:37,755 --> 00:19:40,716
Koreans. Good people.
Know who they are.

405
00:19:41,175 --> 00:19:43,302
A lotta people today don't know
who the heck they are.

406
00:19:43,969 --> 00:19:45,721
A man without knowledge
of his roots

407
00:19:45,930 --> 00:19:47,765
is like a cabbage
in this society.

408
00:19:47,973 --> 00:19:49,016
That's true.

409
00:19:49,475 --> 00:19:50,935
So you deny any connection
to the incidents

410
00:19:51,060 --> 00:19:53,062
- at the Fitzwilliam compound?
- Heck, no.

411
00:19:53,229 --> 00:19:55,481
There's an Aryan soldier
who honors and respects me

412
00:19:55,606 --> 00:19:58,275
inside the compound. He carried
out the mission for me.

413
00:19:58,734 --> 00:20:00,820
I'm just saying I wouldn't
call anyone about it.

414
00:20:01,278 --> 00:20:02,363
That's just dumb.

415
00:20:02,947 --> 00:20:05,032
But I guess there's
a dummy in any group.

416
00:20:05,241 --> 00:20:07,159
Right, Agent Cho?

417
00:20:19,046 --> 00:20:21,048
- Mr. Jane, may I ask...
- Marcus

418
00:20:21,257 --> 00:20:23,134
if I wanted
to break into this compound

419
00:20:23,300 --> 00:20:24,885
where would be
the best place to do it?

420
00:20:25,469 --> 00:20:26,512
Excuse me?

421
00:20:26,971 --> 00:20:28,139
Where's the weak link?

422
00:20:28,597 --> 00:20:30,516
This property is 100% secure.

423
00:20:31,976 --> 00:20:33,853
When you learned someone had
been murdered in the guesthouse

424
00:20:34,019 --> 00:20:35,438
something popped
into your mind...

425
00:20:35,563 --> 00:20:38,399
an image of a location you've been
worried about, a weakness.

426
00:20:38,899 --> 00:20:39,942
What was it?

427
00:20:40,568 --> 00:20:42,236
- No.
- Yes.

428
00:20:44,822 --> 00:20:46,449
- It's nothing, but, uh...
- Go on.

429
00:20:47,491 --> 00:20:48,534
North wall.

430
00:20:49,326 --> 00:20:50,578
Property bends around a gully.

431
00:20:50,745 --> 00:20:52,246
Curve in the wall makes it
hard for the sensors

432
00:20:52,371 --> 00:20:53,414
to pick up movement.

433
00:20:55,416 --> 00:20:56,459
Okay.

434
00:20:58,836 --> 00:20:59,920
You'll need to go through the gate.

435
00:21:00,171 --> 00:21:01,213
Okay. Of course.

436
00:21:05,217 --> 00:21:06,635
This Aryan soldier...
give me a name.

437
00:21:07,178 --> 00:21:09,972
Yeah. No.
Why would I do that?

438
00:21:10,139 --> 00:21:13,058
You've had your revenge already.
Why not give up your man?

439
00:21:14,268 --> 00:21:15,603
Life could be a lot easier
for you in here

440
00:21:15,728 --> 00:21:17,313
if we tell the warden
you're helping us out.

441
00:21:17,605 --> 00:21:19,231
Extra smokes, more yard time?

442
00:21:19,356 --> 00:21:21,567
Yeah. Like that.
Flat screen TV maybe.

443
00:21:22,109 --> 00:21:23,319
You don't understand.

444
00:21:23,486 --> 00:21:26,071
There's honor among us race warriors.

445
00:21:26,363 --> 00:21:28,783
Loyalty. Brotherhood.

446
00:21:29,408 --> 00:21:30,701
Yeah, right.

447
00:21:31,494 --> 00:21:33,829
What do you mean,
"Yeah, right"?

448
00:21:34,288 --> 00:21:35,539
It means you're wasting my time.

449
00:21:35,664 --> 00:21:36,957
You have no one
inside the compound.

450
00:21:37,082 --> 00:21:39,585
There are no Aryan warriors
out there awaiting your orders.

451
00:21:40,878 --> 00:21:42,546
You're a sad little man
alone in a box

452
00:21:42,671 --> 00:21:44,298
living on delusions of grandeur.

453
00:21:44,924 --> 00:21:47,218
You are 100% wrong.

454
00:21:47,384 --> 00:21:49,762
I got an army behind me.
An army!

455
00:21:49,929 --> 00:21:51,430
And I got a guy inside.

456
00:21:52,515 --> 00:21:54,350
- No, you don't.
- Hey, wait a minute!

457
00:21:55,309 --> 00:21:59,355
Howard Dressler is his name.
My guy. Inside.

458
00:21:59,814 --> 00:22:01,398
So choke on that, Cho.

459
00:22:02,233 --> 00:22:04,026
Thanks.
Heil Hitler.

460
00:22:07,822 --> 00:22:10,908
Blood pressure's still high.
So's your heart rate.

461
00:22:11,492 --> 00:22:13,369
I'm gonna give you a Xanax
to help calm you down.

462
00:22:13,536 --> 00:22:15,704
I don't want any medication.
Not today.

463
00:22:18,457 --> 00:22:19,542
Any word on Abby?

464
00:22:20,376 --> 00:22:21,418
No.

465
00:22:22,920 --> 00:22:24,338
Then if you'll excuse me

466
00:22:24,463 --> 00:22:26,674
my mother's funeral
is this afternoon

467
00:22:26,799 --> 00:22:28,968
and I really need
to finish her eulogy.

468
00:22:29,468 --> 00:22:31,053
- I'll come back later.
- Thank you, Ed.

469
00:22:39,019 --> 00:22:40,896
So you're holding
the service here?

470
00:22:41,564 --> 00:22:44,191
Yes. She's being buried
on the property beside my father.

471
00:22:44,358 --> 00:22:45,901
Surprising you're going ahead with it

472
00:22:46,694 --> 00:22:48,737
given recent events.

473
00:22:50,739 --> 00:22:52,616
What would you have me do,
Mr. Jane?

474
00:22:53,909 --> 00:22:56,620
I'm sorry if I'm not behaving
the way you think I should.

475
00:22:56,787 --> 00:22:59,582
It's not every day my mother dies
and my daughter goes missing.

476
00:23:01,458 --> 00:23:02,585
Now if there's...

477
00:23:03,294 --> 00:23:04,545
anything else you need...

478
00:23:07,506 --> 00:23:09,049
- No.
- Good.

479
00:23:10,426 --> 00:23:13,512
- Because I really must finish this.
- By all means.

480
00:23:17,725 --> 00:23:18,767
Hmm.

481
00:23:21,353 --> 00:23:22,730
That's a beautiful rug.

482
00:23:23,355 --> 00:23:25,941
- Thank you.
- It's very nice. Held up well.

483
00:23:27,735 --> 00:23:29,612
Especially having kids in the house.

484
00:23:30,237 --> 00:23:32,281
That's because I never let
the girls play on it.

485
00:23:33,699 --> 00:23:34,825
You said that

486
00:23:35,826 --> 00:23:37,536
but Abby didn't listen
to you, did she?

487
00:23:40,080 --> 00:23:41,123
No.

488
00:23:42,041 --> 00:23:45,377
Whatever she was told not to do
that's exactly what she would do.

489
00:23:45,711 --> 00:23:46,962
Always contrary.

490
00:23:47,588 --> 00:23:49,673
Hard for someone like you
to handle, I imagine.

491
00:23:50,799 --> 00:23:51,884
Someone like me?

492
00:23:52,551 --> 00:23:54,970
Disciplined. Rigorous.

493
00:23:56,055 --> 00:23:58,641
Wound. You are wound.

494
00:23:59,433 --> 00:24:00,893
It wasn't all bad.

495
00:24:03,437 --> 00:24:04,772
She's a beautiful girl.

496
00:24:06,482 --> 00:24:08,651
She's strong and funny...

497
00:24:10,694 --> 00:24:13,447
and we'd grown apart
these past few years because...

498
00:24:14,865 --> 00:24:16,909
Well, ever since my husband died

499
00:24:17,076 --> 00:24:20,037
but even so there were times
when Abby and I were together

500
00:24:20,162 --> 00:24:22,665
and it was as if
she were a girl again and...

501
00:24:23,666 --> 00:24:24,708
we were happy.

502
00:24:29,338 --> 00:24:30,756
She's dead, isn't she?

503
00:24:32,466 --> 00:24:33,801
My daughter's dead.

504
00:24:36,845 --> 00:24:38,263
It's not unlikely.

505
00:24:42,768 --> 00:24:43,811
Excuse me.

506
00:24:52,861 --> 00:24:55,280
- What's this?
- Visitor logs from the security team...

507
00:24:55,489 --> 00:24:57,116
every person who entered
and left the compound

508
00:24:57,282 --> 00:24:58,367
over the last three months.

509
00:24:58,784 --> 00:25:00,244
Lisbon wants us
to look through 'em.

510
00:25:01,745 --> 00:25:04,039
Raymond Tubbs said he had
a man named Howard Dressler

511
00:25:04,164 --> 00:25:05,207
inside the compound.

512
00:25:08,335 --> 00:25:09,378
Is that new?

513
00:25:10,295 --> 00:25:11,922
Oh. Yes.

514
00:25:13,757 --> 00:25:15,342
- It's a gift?
- Uh-huh.

515
00:25:17,553 --> 00:25:18,637
From O'Laughlin, huh?

516
00:25:19,555 --> 00:25:20,597
Uh-huh.

517
00:25:20,806 --> 00:25:21,849
He has good taste.

518
00:25:22,307 --> 00:25:23,350
Thanks.

519
00:25:25,352 --> 00:25:26,395
What was that name again?

520
00:25:26,895 --> 00:25:28,230
Uh, Howard Dressler.

521
00:25:29,732 --> 00:25:30,774
Got him.

522
00:25:31,025 --> 00:25:32,067
Nice.

523
00:25:58,635 --> 00:26:00,220
- What's up?
- "We found Howard Dressler."

524
00:26:00,387 --> 00:26:01,638
"He tried to run
but we caught him."

525
00:26:01,764 --> 00:26:02,973
"We're gonna take him in
now for questioning."

526
00:26:03,140 --> 00:26:05,851
Nice work. I'll call you back.
What's going on?

527
00:26:06,351 --> 00:26:07,519
Perimeter sensor's been tripped.

528
00:26:07,644 --> 00:26:10,272
Someone's trying to break onto
the compound. We're on our way.

529
00:26:11,648 --> 00:26:13,358
CBI!
Don't move!

530
00:26:13,650 --> 00:26:15,444
Turn around slowly
with your hands up.

531
00:26:19,239 --> 00:26:21,158
- Jane?
- Hey, Lisbon.

532
00:26:21,742 --> 00:26:22,785
When did you get here?

533
00:26:33,126 --> 00:26:34,795
Hey, hey, hey.
Jane.

534
00:26:36,379 --> 00:26:37,714
How are you guys doing today?

535
00:26:39,800 --> 00:26:41,093
I, myself...

536
00:26:42,636 --> 00:26:43,929
am having a great day.

537
00:26:45,305 --> 00:26:48,475
I got a call
from a Pauline Fitzwilliam.

538
00:26:49,351 --> 00:26:53,063
A federal judge, Fitzwilliam.

539
00:26:53,605 --> 00:26:55,398
Saying that a CBI consultant

540
00:26:55,524 --> 00:26:57,734
was caught stealing a rug
from her residence.

541
00:26:58,902 --> 00:27:01,613
- Ma'am, I sincerely apologize...
- Oh, hush, Lisbon.

542
00:27:01,738 --> 00:27:04,282
There's no reason to apologize.
I was working the case.

543
00:27:04,866 --> 00:27:05,909
The rug was a stand-in corpse.

544
00:27:06,034 --> 00:27:07,911
I just wanted to see
if it was possible for the killer

545
00:27:08,036 --> 00:27:10,205
to leave the compound
with Abby's body.

546
00:27:10,372 --> 00:27:11,665
And is it possible?

547
00:27:12,332 --> 00:27:14,417
Not unless the culprit
was a mountain gorilla.

548
00:27:17,963 --> 00:27:21,424
So now you've had your fun
to no useful end

549
00:27:21,716 --> 00:27:23,927
and now she's asking me
to remove you from the case.

550
00:27:24,052 --> 00:27:26,555
Is there any reason
why I shouldn't do as she asks?

551
00:27:32,435 --> 00:27:33,520
She's a suspect.

552
00:27:37,315 --> 00:27:38,358
Really?

553
00:27:38,483 --> 00:27:40,068
She hasn't been excluded
has she?

554
00:27:41,111 --> 00:27:42,696
Then she's still a suspect

555
00:27:43,238 --> 00:27:46,366
and it would look bad to be seen
allowing a murder suspect

556
00:27:46,491 --> 00:27:48,910
dictate the terms
of an investigation

557
00:27:49,703 --> 00:27:50,745
right?

558
00:27:52,205 --> 00:27:53,540
Is this true, Lisbon?

559
00:27:54,416 --> 00:27:55,625
Is she a suspect?

560
00:27:56,334 --> 00:27:57,711
She has not been excluded.

561
00:27:59,921 --> 00:28:00,964
Okay.

562
00:28:01,464 --> 00:28:02,757
I'll give you some more rope.

563
00:28:03,633 --> 00:28:04,926
Don't hang yourself with it.

564
00:28:05,719 --> 00:28:07,429
And, you know
next time call me

565
00:28:08,305 --> 00:28:09,931
when you wanna do
some more foolishness.

566
00:28:10,056 --> 00:28:11,433
"Foolishness," I think
is a little harsh...

567
00:28:11,558 --> 00:28:13,727
- Go.
- Okay, I'm leaving.

568
00:28:14,769 --> 00:28:15,854
I have your numbers.

569
00:28:19,107 --> 00:28:20,984
Come on, Howard.
Don't lie to me.

570
00:28:21,568 --> 00:28:22,944
Already spoke to Raymond Tubbs.

571
00:28:24,070 --> 00:28:25,113
Raymond Tubbs?

572
00:28:26,281 --> 00:28:28,325
- What about him?
- Well, you tell me.

573
00:28:29,451 --> 00:28:31,077
He's an American patriot.

574
00:28:32,787 --> 00:28:34,497
I subscribe
to some of his newsletters.

575
00:28:34,664 --> 00:28:35,832
There's no crime in that.

576
00:28:36,291 --> 00:28:38,710
Well, Tubbs says you're his guy
inside the Fitzwilliam compound.

577
00:28:39,502 --> 00:28:41,004
Says that you're the, uh...

578
00:28:41,171 --> 00:28:43,715
"Aryan warrior that avenged
his unjust imprisonment"

579
00:28:44,090 --> 00:28:46,676
- killed Austin Marr.
- Whoa. I had nothing to do with that.

580
00:28:46,801 --> 00:28:47,928
Okay. If you say so.

581
00:28:48,678 --> 00:28:50,847
But you can see how it looks.
Not good.

582
00:28:52,140 --> 00:28:55,477
No, no, no. I keep my business
and my politics totally separate.

583
00:28:55,602 --> 00:28:56,895
Oh, the Third Reich Pool
Cleaning Company

584
00:28:57,020 --> 00:28:58,313
doesn't play so good, huh?

585
00:29:00,774 --> 00:29:03,443
I've exchanged a few
e-mails with Tubbs. That's all.

586
00:29:03,902 --> 00:29:05,612
If he says any different
he's lying.

587
00:29:10,450 --> 00:29:12,661
I got immunity for what
I say in here, right?

588
00:29:12,994 --> 00:29:14,037
No.

589
00:29:16,915 --> 00:29:19,125
Okay. Occasionally...

590
00:29:20,585 --> 00:29:22,003
I got stuff for Abby.

591
00:29:22,629 --> 00:29:25,090
Stuff? You sold her drugs?

592
00:29:26,049 --> 00:29:28,385
A little coke. Some meth.

593
00:29:28,551 --> 00:29:29,928
When was the last time
you scored for her?

594
00:29:30,553 --> 00:29:31,638
Not for a couple of months

595
00:29:31,763 --> 00:29:33,640
but then the other day
she hit me up.

596
00:29:33,807 --> 00:29:35,350
She was in a real bad way.

597
00:29:35,475 --> 00:29:39,271
She asked me for an eight ball
and some downers.

598
00:29:39,437 --> 00:29:41,356
It took me a few days
but I got 'em.

599
00:29:42,524 --> 00:29:44,234
But the morning I showed up
there was cops everywhere.

600
00:29:44,359 --> 00:29:45,860
I didn't even get
to give 'em to her.

601
00:29:47,946 --> 00:29:51,074
Look, I know I screwed up
but I didn't kill Austin.

602
00:29:52,826 --> 00:29:54,577
There was a useful end
by the way.

603
00:29:55,328 --> 00:29:58,164
We now know for sure that nobody
entered or left the property

604
00:29:58,290 --> 00:30:00,083
the night of the murder
so she must've been murdered

605
00:30:00,208 --> 00:30:01,876
in the guest room
along with Austin.

606
00:30:02,002 --> 00:30:04,004
Then the killer hid her body.

607
00:30:04,254 --> 00:30:05,839
We searched.
She's not on the compound.

608
00:30:06,006 --> 00:30:07,716
You searched for a living,
breathing woman

609
00:30:07,841 --> 00:30:09,467
and not a dead body.
Big difference.

610
00:30:09,592 --> 00:30:11,428
Why would the killer hide
one victim

611
00:30:11,553 --> 00:30:12,595
and leave the other one behind?

612
00:30:12,721 --> 00:30:13,763
Good question.

613
00:30:14,639 --> 00:30:15,682
We'll search the property again.

614
00:30:15,807 --> 00:30:17,600
This time we'll get cadaver dogs
and more personnel.

615
00:30:19,352 --> 00:30:21,563
No need. I know exactly
where the body is hidden.

616
00:30:23,481 --> 00:30:24,858
Wait. Wait.
What are you gonna do?

617
00:30:25,108 --> 00:30:26,151
Just talk.

618
00:30:26,276 --> 00:30:27,319
But they're in the middle
of the funeral.

619
00:30:27,444 --> 00:30:28,820
You can't just walk
in there willy-nilly.

620
00:30:29,863 --> 00:30:31,406
- Yeah. That's right.
- Thank you.

621
00:30:32,532 --> 00:30:35,035
- I forgot to call Hightower.
- Hightower? Why?

622
00:30:36,536 --> 00:30:39,080
Voice mail.
Hey, Hightower. It's Jane.

623
00:30:39,205 --> 00:30:41,333
Just wanted to let you know
that, uh, there's gonna be

624
00:30:41,458 --> 00:30:43,084
what you like to call
"foolishness" going on

625
00:30:43,209 --> 00:30:44,627
at Ethel Sebring's funeral.

626
00:30:45,128 --> 00:30:46,880
That's it. Have a great day.

627
00:30:48,214 --> 00:30:49,466
She told me to call.

628
00:30:50,967 --> 00:30:52,302
- Better hurry.
- Jane.

629
00:30:53,261 --> 00:30:54,304
Jane.

630
00:30:55,138 --> 00:30:56,264
God, our father

631
00:30:57,057 --> 00:30:59,017
your power brings us to birth.

632
00:30:59,434 --> 00:31:01,853
Your Providence guides
our lives

633
00:31:02,187 --> 00:31:05,106
and by your command
we return to dust.

634
00:31:05,607 --> 00:31:07,359
Unite us together in one family

635
00:31:07,484 --> 00:31:10,653
to sing your praise forever
and ever. Amen.

636
00:31:11,237 --> 00:31:13,448
In the name of the father
and of the son

637
00:31:13,615 --> 00:31:16,076
and of the holy spirit, amen.

638
00:31:16,242 --> 00:31:17,494
Amen. Thank you, father.

639
00:31:18,244 --> 00:31:19,746
Uh, good afternoon
ladies and gentlemen.

640
00:31:19,871 --> 00:31:21,122
My name is Patrick Jane.

641
00:31:21,247 --> 00:31:22,415
For those of you
who don't know me

642
00:31:22,540 --> 00:31:25,210
I am a consultant with the CBI.

643
00:31:25,752 --> 00:31:29,672
I know that you're all here today
to mourn the loss of Ethel Sebring

644
00:31:30,173 --> 00:31:31,925
but I have a very important announcement

645
00:31:32,133 --> 00:31:34,552
- that simply can't wait.
- What is the meaning of this?

646
00:31:34,677 --> 00:31:37,013
Uh, just bear with me
please, for one moment.

647
00:31:37,764 --> 00:31:39,391
Well, there's no easy way
to say this

648
00:31:39,516 --> 00:31:41,351
so I'm just gonna
come straight out with it.

649
00:31:41,976 --> 00:31:43,686
Abby Fitzwilliam is dead.

650
00:31:44,270 --> 00:31:45,397
No.

651
00:31:45,522 --> 00:31:48,858
Yeah, it's true, Sophie.
I'm... I'm very sorry for your loss.

652
00:31:50,985 --> 00:31:52,028
How?

653
00:31:52,153 --> 00:31:53,863
We don't know all the details
as yet

654
00:31:53,988 --> 00:31:55,865
but we will know very soon.

655
00:31:57,575 --> 00:31:58,618
Where is she?

656
00:32:03,706 --> 00:32:05,875
She's hidden
in your grandmother's casket.

657
00:32:07,794 --> 00:32:10,964
It's quite clever, actually. It's... it's
one place you wouldn't look for a body

658
00:32:11,506 --> 00:32:14,759
other than the obvious
exception, of course.

659
00:32:15,051 --> 00:32:17,178
Are you playing
some sort of demented joke?

660
00:32:17,846 --> 00:32:19,764
I wish I could say I was.
Uh...

661
00:32:21,724 --> 00:32:23,017
They were both small women.

662
00:32:23,643 --> 00:32:26,271
They could fit comfortably
together in this box.

663
00:32:26,855 --> 00:32:28,440
The only way we can tell for sure

664
00:32:29,524 --> 00:32:30,942
is if we, uh...

665
00:32:35,238 --> 00:32:36,865
Well, we're gonna have to take
a quick peek.

666
00:32:37,574 --> 00:32:40,493
Um, we... we will do it inside.

667
00:32:40,994 --> 00:32:43,413
Dr. Saban will oversee proceedings

668
00:32:43,538 --> 00:32:45,999
to make sure
that everything is shipshape.

669
00:32:46,166 --> 00:32:49,002
Agent, have you no control
over this buffoon?

670
00:32:49,169 --> 00:32:51,296
Lisbon, trust me.
You gotta trust me on this one.

671
00:32:54,174 --> 00:32:56,342
Mr. Jane is making
a valid point.

672
00:32:56,593 --> 00:32:58,344
Ma'am, you know more
about the law than we do.

673
00:32:58,470 --> 00:32:59,929
We can get a warrant but...

674
00:33:00,555 --> 00:33:03,099
I think this will be quicker
and less intrusive

675
00:33:04,601 --> 00:33:06,394
with all due respect.

676
00:33:14,819 --> 00:33:15,862
This is wrong.

677
00:33:16,154 --> 00:33:18,865
- Oh, please.
- Ethel was dignified in life.

678
00:33:18,990 --> 00:33:20,742
She'd want to remain so
in death.

679
00:33:20,992 --> 00:33:24,037
Doctor, you of all people should know
there's nothing dignified about death.

680
00:33:24,329 --> 00:33:25,371
What's going on?

681
00:33:26,372 --> 00:33:27,415
Oh.

682
00:33:27,916 --> 00:33:30,502
- You got my message.
- Ma'am, everything is under control.

683
00:33:31,127 --> 00:33:33,922
- What's he doing to that casket?
- Well, that's what I was calling you about.

684
00:33:34,088 --> 00:33:36,591
Opening it? Jane says
that Abby Fitzwilliam's body

685
00:33:36,716 --> 00:33:37,759
is in the casket.

686
00:33:37,884 --> 00:33:41,179
Oh, my God.
Have you gone completely insane?

687
00:33:41,429 --> 00:33:42,722
No, I don't think so.

688
00:33:43,598 --> 00:33:44,641
There we go.

689
00:33:47,101 --> 00:33:48,603
Pauline, are you sure
you wanna do this?

690
00:33:48,728 --> 00:33:50,104
Just get it over with.

691
00:33:57,946 --> 00:33:58,988
What?

692
00:33:59,197 --> 00:34:00,240
Oh.

693
00:34:01,699 --> 00:34:02,742
Oh, no.

694
00:34:23,386 --> 00:34:25,888
The guests have been sent home.
The funeral's been postponed.

695
00:34:26,013 --> 00:34:28,391
- I hope you're happy.
- Oh, it doesn't make sense.

696
00:34:29,225 --> 00:34:32,395
Abby's body is not in this coffin.
You promised me.

697
00:34:32,520 --> 00:34:35,481
Yeah, I thought she was.
I was certain that she was in there.

698
00:34:35,606 --> 00:34:36,649
Well, you were wrong.

699
00:34:36,774 --> 00:34:38,401
Well, it doesn't make sense
that I was wrong.

700
00:34:38,901 --> 00:34:40,278
Stop saying that!

701
00:34:40,403 --> 00:34:42,154
But this is the perfect place
to hide the body.

702
00:34:42,280 --> 00:34:44,323
It's the one place
that no one would think to look.

703
00:34:44,490 --> 00:34:45,575
Jane, that's enough.

704
00:34:46,075 --> 00:34:48,619
No, w... she's on this compound.
I know that.

705
00:34:48,744 --> 00:34:50,496
- I know that she's on this compound.
- Jane.

706
00:34:50,621 --> 00:34:53,666
We need to get the sniffer dogs
and the helicopters and...

707
00:34:53,791 --> 00:34:56,752
'cause she is here.
I am so sorry.

708
00:34:57,712 --> 00:34:58,754
Sorry.

709
00:34:59,589 --> 00:35:01,299
Okay. All right.
Um...

710
00:35:02,425 --> 00:35:04,135
At first light tomorrow

711
00:35:04,760 --> 00:35:07,805
I want you to start a comprehensive
search for Abby's body.

712
00:35:08,306 --> 00:35:11,309
If she's here, find her.

713
00:35:17,189 --> 00:35:18,232
She's here.

714
00:35:18,816 --> 00:35:20,151
Lisbon, what were you thinking?

715
00:35:20,693 --> 00:35:23,029
I was... no excuses, ma'am.

716
00:35:23,154 --> 00:35:24,697
He asked me to trust him
and I did.

717
00:35:24,822 --> 00:35:26,574
Your job is not to trust him.

718
00:35:26,907 --> 00:35:29,660
Your job is to trust
your judgment, not his.

719
00:35:31,787 --> 00:35:33,247
That poor woman
was in the ground.

720
00:35:33,456 --> 00:35:35,541
Not in the ground
but on her way.

721
00:35:35,666 --> 00:35:36,876
I mean, aren't we all on our way?

722
00:35:37,001 --> 00:35:40,171
You have messed with the funeral
of a high court judge's mother

723
00:35:40,296 --> 00:35:44,008
on the very day she finds out
that her daughter is most likely dead.

724
00:35:44,634 --> 00:35:48,638
That is a very bad career move
for all of us.

725
00:35:51,015 --> 00:35:53,851
Sorry if I got you guys into trouble.
I made a mistake.

726
00:35:54,018 --> 00:35:55,186
Oh, I'm sorry.
Say that again.

727
00:35:55,311 --> 00:35:58,314
I made a mistake. I said it twice.
I won't say it again.

728
00:35:58,439 --> 00:35:59,565
Because it just now occurs to me

729
00:35:59,690 --> 00:36:01,901
that perhaps I'll be proven not quite
as wrong as I appear to be

730
00:36:02,026 --> 00:36:03,361
- in this very moment.
- Is that right?

731
00:36:03,486 --> 00:36:05,780
Yes. In fact, I'm sure of it.
So don't worry.

732
00:36:06,155 --> 00:36:07,198
Your careers are safe.

733
00:36:07,323 --> 00:36:10,326
Judge Fitzwilliam will change her tune
once I reveal her daughter's killer.

734
00:36:10,451 --> 00:36:11,494
Won't she?

735
00:36:11,952 --> 00:36:14,664
I imagine she will.
When do you plan on doing that?

736
00:36:14,830 --> 00:36:16,624
- This very evening.
- This very night?

737
00:36:16,749 --> 00:36:18,000
But you have to trust me.

738
00:36:18,209 --> 00:36:19,669
Right. And what if you're wrong again?

739
00:36:19,794 --> 00:36:21,671
Well, if I'm wrong
then we're in deep trouble.

740
00:36:21,796 --> 00:36:23,422
But what are the chances, really

741
00:36:23,589 --> 00:36:25,549
of me being wrong
twice in a row?

742
00:36:25,883 --> 00:36:26,926
Think about that one.

743
00:36:28,427 --> 00:36:30,680
Of course, if either of you
have a better idea

744
00:36:30,805 --> 00:36:33,766
how to find Abby's body
and catch her killer, please.

745
00:36:33,891 --> 00:36:35,768
These are not taxi doors,
they're ears.

746
00:36:51,742 --> 00:36:53,703
It's not gonna work
unless you're quiet.

747
00:36:53,911 --> 00:36:56,747
I can't keep quiet.
My legs are asleep.

748
00:37:00,459 --> 00:37:02,420
What do you mean
your legs are asleep?

749
00:37:03,587 --> 00:37:05,047
Legs don't sleep.

750
00:37:05,464 --> 00:37:07,842
It's absurd. I don't know
why people say that.

751
00:38:00,019 --> 00:38:01,061
Damn.

752
00:38:02,188 --> 00:38:03,230
Damn.

753
00:38:06,192 --> 00:38:07,359
Where the hell is it?

754
00:38:30,174 --> 00:38:31,217
Hello?

755
00:38:31,342 --> 00:38:32,384
"What's up, Doc?"

756
00:38:33,594 --> 00:38:35,054
Put your hands in the air!

757
00:38:36,806 --> 00:38:38,516
Sorry.
Did we scare you?

758
00:38:42,436 --> 00:38:45,439
You hid Abby's body, and not Austin's
because you had to.

759
00:38:46,190 --> 00:38:48,442
Evidence of your guilt
was inside Abby.

760
00:38:49,443 --> 00:38:52,154
Come on. We both know
the autopsy will confirm it.

761
00:38:52,530 --> 00:38:53,906
You were giving Abby drugs.

762
00:38:59,411 --> 00:39:01,247
A few days before Ethel died

763
00:39:01,956 --> 00:39:03,332
"Abby relapsed."

764
00:39:04,708 --> 00:39:05,835
"She was an addict."

765
00:39:07,169 --> 00:39:10,965
She was either gonna get her drugs
from me or from the street.

766
00:39:12,800 --> 00:39:14,426
"I was managing her addiction."

767
00:39:16,762 --> 00:39:19,181
"It's recognized
therapeutic practice."

768
00:39:19,849 --> 00:39:21,141
For which you were paid.

769
00:39:21,725 --> 00:39:23,602
Well, yes, of course.
I'm a doctor.

770
00:39:23,978 --> 00:39:27,398
"Of course. So you weren't
doing it to help Abby out."

771
00:39:27,565 --> 00:39:28,816
You were doing it
for the money.

772
00:39:30,109 --> 00:39:32,319
With Ethel dying, you needed
a new source of income.

773
00:39:32,444 --> 00:39:34,864
"Then along came Abby
a rich, young addict."

774
00:39:38,409 --> 00:39:40,661
"Abby, it's okay.
You're okay."

775
00:39:41,579 --> 00:39:44,957
"You're okay. Abby.
Abby, stay with me. Abby."

776
00:39:45,499 --> 00:39:47,751
"Abby. Abby, stay with me."

777
00:39:49,086 --> 00:39:50,880
She OD'd so fast.

778
00:39:51,547 --> 00:39:52,673
I couldn't save her.

779
00:39:56,218 --> 00:39:57,553
Austin came back.

780
00:39:58,804 --> 00:40:00,514
- "What's going on?"
- "Saw what had happened."

781
00:40:00,931 --> 00:40:02,141
"What... what'd you do to her?"

782
00:40:02,349 --> 00:40:03,976
He was gonna go to the police.

783
00:40:04,977 --> 00:40:06,020
Turn me in.

784
00:40:09,773 --> 00:40:12,276
My whole life was over
if he made that call.

785
00:40:14,236 --> 00:40:15,321
I picked up the knife

786
00:40:15,779 --> 00:40:18,115
"just to stop him
not to hurt him."

787
00:40:20,534 --> 00:40:21,577
"I wasn't thinking."

788
00:40:26,290 --> 00:40:29,543
I figured if I made it look
like Abby did it...

789
00:40:31,045 --> 00:40:32,463
"people would believe it."

790
00:40:37,843 --> 00:40:41,639
I knew if they found Abby's body
they'd find the drugs in her system.

791
00:40:42,932 --> 00:40:45,976
So I hid her in my room
in the closet.

792
00:40:46,977 --> 00:40:49,688
I was so scared when the police
came to search the house.

793
00:40:50,648 --> 00:40:52,024
I was sure they'd find her.

794
00:40:53,776 --> 00:40:55,319
You took advantage of Abby.

795
00:40:56,153 --> 00:40:57,780
She trusted you
and you preyed on her

796
00:40:57,905 --> 00:40:59,365
in her weakest moment.

797
00:41:00,908 --> 00:41:02,201
She never had a chance.

798
00:41:10,960 --> 00:41:12,920
- Hey.
- Mm?

799
00:41:14,213 --> 00:41:16,340
So I just talked
to Judge Fitzwilliam.

800
00:41:16,757 --> 00:41:18,467
- And?
- And she says

801
00:41:18,634 --> 00:41:21,261
that if you will apologize
for the cavalier manner

802
00:41:21,387 --> 00:41:24,056
with which you disrupted
her mother's burial

803
00:41:24,682 --> 00:41:27,309
she will not pursue
disciplinary action against you

804
00:41:27,685 --> 00:41:29,687
or Lisbon or myself.

805
00:41:30,020 --> 00:41:32,564
Hmm. Tell her Jane says

806
00:41:32,773 --> 00:41:35,401
she's a self-righteous
embittered old bat

807
00:41:35,526 --> 00:41:38,112
- and she should thank me.
- Oh, God, Jane, please.

808
00:41:38,529 --> 00:41:39,863
You're right, Mr. Jane.

809
00:41:42,408 --> 00:41:44,368
I came here for an apology

810
00:41:45,786 --> 00:41:48,831
but I realize now I was wrong
to stand on my dignity.

811
00:41:50,916 --> 00:41:52,001
I am embittered.

812
00:41:53,252 --> 00:41:56,797
And your arrogant, callous
juvenile behavior

813
00:41:56,922 --> 00:41:59,008
did reveal the truth after all
so...

814
00:42:00,759 --> 00:42:01,802
Thank you.

815
00:42:02,594 --> 00:42:03,804
Thank you very much.

816
00:42:05,514 --> 00:42:07,725
- Good evening to you.
- Good evening.

817
00:42:11,979 --> 00:42:13,022
Sorry.

818
00:42:17,276 --> 00:42:18,318
Okay, then.

819
00:42:20,738 --> 00:42:21,780
Everyone's happy.

